1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:30,000
= kissasia.co =

2
00:00:50,154 --> 00:00:53,324
THE ORDINARY JACKPOT

3
00:01:00,039 --> 00:01:01,707
We live within time.

4
00:01:08,506 --> 00:01:10,758
Time doesn't discriminate
between the rich and poor

5
00:01:11,175 --> 00:01:12,385
the good and evil

6
00:01:12,927 --> 00:01:14,762
or the young and the old.

7
00:01:15,262 --> 00:01:16,931
Time passes equally for everyone.

8
00:01:52,091 --> 00:01:54,260
I live the time I'm given.

9
00:01:54,719 --> 00:01:57,179
Today passes just like yesterday

10
00:01:57,847 --> 00:01:59,306
and tomorrow will be no different.

11
00:02:01,267 --> 00:02:02,518
Today, as always

12
00:02:03,352 --> 00:02:04,520
time passes us by

13
00:02:05,479 --> 00:02:06,939
so indifferently.

14
00:02:44,143 --> 00:02:49,064
EPISODE 1: GOOD THINGS COME
TO THOSE WHO WAIT

15
00:03:02,912 --> 00:03:04,579
Good morning, Mr. Gong.

16
00:03:04,580 --> 00:03:05,915
Morning, Ji-hye.

17
00:03:12,463 --> 00:03:13,797
- Morning.
- You just got here?

18
00:03:13,798 --> 00:03:15,424
Yes, I ran a bit late.

19
00:03:16,050 --> 00:03:17,342
Times have changed.

20
00:03:17,343 --> 00:03:19,261
Good morning, everyone.

21
00:03:20,012 --> 00:03:21,180
Hi, Gong.

22
00:03:22,681 --> 00:03:24,098
Good morning, Mr. Gong.

23
00:03:24,099 --> 00:03:25,476
- Morning, Gi-tae.
- Hi.

24
00:03:26,977 --> 00:03:29,271
- When did you get here?
- Five minutes ago.

25
00:03:40,491 --> 00:03:41,909
Hello, good morning.

26
00:03:44,411 --> 00:03:46,831
- You feel okay this morning?
- I'm totally fine.

27
00:03:48,541 --> 00:03:49,959
- Hello, Mr. Jeong.
- Hi.

28
00:03:52,711 --> 00:03:53,795
Hello, Mr. Yang.

29
00:03:53,796 --> 00:03:55,422
- Hello.
- Good morning.

30
00:03:56,590 --> 00:03:58,676
- Good morning, Mr. Yang.
- Good morning.

31
00:04:06,350 --> 00:04:09,394
- Hey, Ju-hui.
- Good morning.

32
00:04:09,395 --> 00:04:11,771
What happened to the outlet manager
who kicked up a fuss?

33
00:04:11,772 --> 00:04:14,274
- How did you know?
- I know everything.

34
00:04:14,275 --> 00:04:16,568
You can run,
but you can't hide from me.

35
00:04:16,569 --> 00:04:17,862
Let's start the meeting.

36
00:04:18,404 --> 00:04:19,446
- Okay.
- Sure.

37
00:04:28,873 --> 00:04:30,748
Mr. Yang, it's time for our meeting.

38
00:04:30,749 --> 00:04:33,001
- Coffee?
- Pardon? Well...

39
00:04:33,002 --> 00:04:34,836
I think you should come over now.

40
00:04:34,837 --> 00:04:37,423
Can I at least get a coffee
to survive the day?

41
00:04:38,132 --> 00:04:39,466
- Fine, I'm coming.
- Good.

42
00:04:40,092 --> 00:04:41,093
I'm coming.

43
00:04:53,522 --> 00:04:55,148
I'll be quick so we can get to work.

44
00:04:55,149 --> 00:04:56,232
- Okay.
- Okay.

45
00:04:56,233 --> 00:04:57,817
Any updates on the discrepancy

46
00:04:57,818 --> 00:04:59,903
between the distribution
and what the mall got?

47
00:04:59,904 --> 00:05:03,072
The mall staff forgot to count
a box they had in storage.

48
00:05:03,073 --> 00:05:04,867
The numbers add up now.

49
00:05:06,118 --> 00:05:07,244
They won't, though.

50
00:05:07,786 --> 00:05:09,287
They still resort to borrowing stock

51
00:05:09,288 --> 00:05:11,415
from other stores
if the numbers don't add up.

52
00:05:11,832 --> 00:05:13,375
You should conduct a spot inspection.

53
00:05:13,667 --> 00:05:14,792
Okay, I'll do that.

54
00:05:14,793 --> 00:05:16,211
Why don't we let it drop this time?

55
00:05:17,212 --> 00:05:19,756
It's obvious they borrowed stock
from another store.

56
00:05:19,757 --> 00:05:22,383
Pointing that out
will only ruffle feathers.

57
00:05:22,384 --> 00:05:24,302
Once sales stabilize

58
00:05:24,303 --> 00:05:26,263
we can check all the remaining stock.

59
00:05:28,891 --> 00:05:29,892
Let's do that, then.

60
00:05:31,018 --> 00:05:33,227
I'll revise the schedule
to reflect that.

61
00:05:33,228 --> 00:05:35,647
Each brand's
projected spring, summer lineup.

62
00:05:35,648 --> 00:05:37,691
I'd like the full list this week.
Can it be done?

63
00:05:41,570 --> 00:05:44,198
- Mr. Yang.
- I'll tell you when it's ready.

64
00:05:44,990 --> 00:05:47,867
We need the list by this week
so we can review it internally

65
00:05:47,868 --> 00:05:49,787
before we place the orders next week.

66
00:05:50,204 --> 00:05:52,831
There's a limit
to what's within my control.

67
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:57,169
Still, check with the brands for me.

68
00:05:58,712 --> 00:05:59,713
Okay.

69
00:06:06,679 --> 00:06:08,179
- Ji-hye.
- Yes?

70
00:06:08,180 --> 00:06:10,848
Some brands are changing their CI.
Share the drafts with me

71
00:06:10,849 --> 00:06:13,852
and compile a questionnaire
to collect input for a future report.

72
00:06:14,311 --> 00:06:15,687
Can you do that by today?

73
00:06:15,688 --> 00:06:16,854
Yes, I can.

74
00:06:16,855 --> 00:06:18,898
Let me know if it's too much.
I'll help.

75
00:06:18,899 --> 00:06:20,401
Not at all. I can manage.

76
00:06:22,569 --> 00:06:26,949
There's also concern that employees
are managing their time too freely.

77
00:06:27,241 --> 00:06:28,409
The work we do

78
00:06:28,701 --> 00:06:30,952
makes it impossible to work
exactly from nine to six

79
00:06:30,953 --> 00:06:33,788
but I'd like you to follow
company rules as best you can.

80
00:06:33,789 --> 00:06:35,081
- Do you all understand?
- Yes.

81
00:06:35,082 --> 00:06:36,083
Yes.

82
00:06:42,172 --> 00:06:43,549
- Let's get to work, then.
- Okay.

83
00:06:45,384 --> 00:06:46,593
Goodness...

84
00:06:48,012 --> 00:06:49,763
You never get a break, do you?

85
00:06:50,597 --> 00:06:53,058
You can train and mentor the juniors

86
00:06:53,559 --> 00:06:55,936
but you have one troublemaker
of an assistant manager.

87
00:06:56,311 --> 00:06:58,479
Mr. Yang must have
struggles of his own.

88
00:06:58,480 --> 00:07:00,940
It can't be easy
working under a younger guy.

89
00:07:00,941 --> 00:07:02,901
True. It's tough on both of you.

90
00:07:03,902 --> 00:07:04,903
What's this meeting about?

91
00:07:05,237 --> 00:07:08,157
I have no idea
what the higher-ups are thinking.

92
00:07:09,408 --> 00:07:10,451
Oh, shoot.

93
00:07:10,993 --> 00:07:12,118
Where are you going?

94
00:07:12,119 --> 00:07:14,454
- It's my leg day.
- What do you mean?

95
00:07:14,455 --> 00:07:15,538
Let's take the stairs.

96
00:07:15,539 --> 00:07:16,957
RESERVATIONS
FOR 4TH-FLOOR CONFERENCE ROOM

97
00:07:20,294 --> 00:07:21,295
Hello.

98
00:07:21,920 --> 00:07:22,921
Hello.

99
00:07:23,756 --> 00:07:24,757
Hello.

100
00:07:25,758 --> 00:07:27,550
- Mr. Jeong?
- Yes?

101
00:07:27,551 --> 00:07:29,720
Am I a zombie, or are you a rat?

102
00:07:30,554 --> 00:07:31,929
What do you mean?

103
00:07:31,930 --> 00:07:33,890
Why did you take the stairs

104
00:07:33,891 --> 00:07:35,683
when the elevator
was working just fine?

105
00:07:35,684 --> 00:07:36,769
Oh, you saw us?

106
00:07:37,436 --> 00:07:40,063
Mr. Gong and I had
something to discuss.

107
00:07:40,064 --> 00:07:42,899
I wonder if you're still ticked off
because I rejected

108
00:07:42,900 --> 00:07:43,901
a few of your ideas.

109
00:07:44,193 --> 00:07:45,611
Did you reject a few ideas?

110
00:07:45,986 --> 00:07:47,321
Why don't I remember that?

111
00:07:47,696 --> 00:07:48,697
Did he?

112
00:07:51,492 --> 00:07:53,077
- Hello, sir.
- Hello, sir.

113
00:07:53,786 --> 00:07:55,496
- You're all here.
- Yes.

114
00:07:56,789 --> 00:07:58,040
- You can sit.
- Thanks.

115
00:08:04,046 --> 00:08:05,047
Okay.

116
00:08:05,380 --> 00:08:08,424
Did you talk to your teams
about managing their time?

117
00:08:08,425 --> 00:08:09,634
- Yes.
- Yes.

118
00:08:09,635 --> 00:08:12,762
Someone will get caught first.
Don't let that be you.

119
00:08:12,763 --> 00:08:14,430
I can't cover for you then.

120
00:08:14,431 --> 00:08:15,598
- Okay.
- Okay.

121
00:08:15,599 --> 00:08:16,892
Let's get things started.

122
00:08:17,935 --> 00:08:19,603
Today's agenda is very simple.

123
00:08:20,771 --> 00:08:21,772
Laknes.

124
00:08:25,776 --> 00:08:27,236
What do you all think about it?

125
00:08:31,573 --> 00:08:33,075
Shall we go clockwise?

126
00:08:33,408 --> 00:08:35,202
Or play rock-paper-scissors?

127
00:08:38,455 --> 00:08:43,043
Their designs are one thing,
but their prices are extremely high.

128
00:08:43,710 --> 00:08:46,754
They're not that well-known
and have a small collection.

129
00:08:46,755 --> 00:08:48,756
And they don't have
that many patterns, either.

130
00:08:48,757 --> 00:08:50,926
I believe
it's a hard brand to launch.

131
00:08:52,344 --> 00:08:53,345
What else?

132
00:08:53,971 --> 00:08:56,849
I believe they just exited
the Korean market.

133
00:08:57,266 --> 00:09:01,310
Unless they've changed
their designs or pricing

134
00:09:01,311 --> 00:09:04,189
won't the result be the same
if we bring them back?

135
00:09:06,483 --> 00:09:08,652
Their designs were hard
to swallow at first.

136
00:09:09,069 --> 00:09:10,736
But times have changed.

137
00:09:10,737 --> 00:09:12,405
They didn't exit
because they flopped.

138
00:09:12,406 --> 00:09:14,782
I think they even got
into the top ten of luxury brands.

139
00:09:14,783 --> 00:09:16,785
Didn't they reach ninth?

140
00:09:17,911 --> 00:09:19,413
Yes, just once.

141
00:09:19,788 --> 00:09:21,582
I get what you're all worried about.

142
00:09:21,874 --> 00:09:23,083
We must do this.

143
00:09:23,667 --> 00:09:24,793
It's our director's order.

144
00:09:25,502 --> 00:09:27,546
Don't take it. Fight back.

145
00:09:29,298 --> 00:09:31,508
Laknes is known
for its radical designs.

146
00:09:32,509 --> 00:09:34,136
Why don't you take it, Mr. Gong?

147
00:09:34,678 --> 00:09:36,679
You're the youngest here
and have the best eye for aesthetics.

148
00:09:36,680 --> 00:09:37,681
No?

149
00:09:40,934 --> 00:09:45,355
As you know, my team doesn't have
the time or bandwidth.

150
00:09:45,814 --> 00:09:48,942
We're the smallest team,
but we handle the most brands.

151
00:09:49,610 --> 00:09:51,195
What do the others think?

152
00:09:53,071 --> 00:09:54,072
Well...

153
00:09:54,406 --> 00:09:57,492
The truth is,
every team is stretched thin.

154
00:09:58,118 --> 00:10:01,622
The team best-suited for the job
would be Mr. Gong's.

155
00:10:02,289 --> 00:10:03,332
You think so too?

156
00:10:05,292 --> 00:10:08,670
I mean, you all have a point

157
00:10:08,921 --> 00:10:13,759
but I fear you're giving him too much
because he's the youngest.

158
00:10:14,301 --> 00:10:15,677
Then Team 4 should take it.

159
00:10:16,220 --> 00:10:18,222
That's not what I meant.

160
00:10:18,931 --> 00:10:20,682
- Mr. Gong.
- Yes?

161
00:10:21,308 --> 00:10:22,643
How about you take Laknes

162
00:10:23,185 --> 00:10:27,022
and give a few brands
to some other teams here?

163
00:10:28,106 --> 00:10:29,316
Can you do it, then?

164
00:10:30,817 --> 00:10:31,818
Yes.

165
00:10:32,861 --> 00:10:34,029
Then we can do it.

166
00:10:36,698 --> 00:10:38,575
Stupid, I told you not to take it.

167
00:10:39,534 --> 00:10:41,203
You're out of your mind.

168
00:10:47,751 --> 00:10:49,961
Why did you give in
when I told you not to?

169
00:10:49,962 --> 00:10:51,463
- Whatever.
- Hey.

170
00:10:51,880 --> 00:10:54,508
If that's not what you meant,
what did you mean?

171
00:10:55,050 --> 00:10:57,844
I tried to defend you
because they all wanted you to...

172
00:10:58,595 --> 00:11:00,389
Gong, can I have a word?

173
00:11:01,265 --> 00:11:04,350
Before you hand over
some of your brands

174
00:11:04,351 --> 00:11:06,144
can you talk to me first?

175
00:11:10,190 --> 00:11:11,233
Yes, of course.

176
00:11:11,650 --> 00:11:13,527
- Let's have a drink soon.
- Sure.

177
00:11:20,742 --> 00:11:21,743
Mr. Kim.

178
00:11:24,037 --> 00:11:25,371
What's this?

179
00:11:25,372 --> 00:11:27,331
It got returned.
Give it to your wife.

180
00:11:27,332 --> 00:11:29,209
Oh, it's a scarf.

181
00:11:30,252 --> 00:11:31,295
Do you think Laknes will work?

182
00:11:31,753 --> 00:11:32,837
Of course not.

183
00:11:32,838 --> 00:11:35,799
We're bringing back a brand
that flopped with zero changes.

184
00:11:36,758 --> 00:11:39,970
Isn't it a jerk move to dump
a sure-fire flop on another team?

185
00:11:40,554 --> 00:11:43,140
I can only go along
with what Mr. Jang suggests.

186
00:11:43,432 --> 00:11:44,557
What else can I do?

187
00:11:44,558 --> 00:11:46,893
You're way too ambitious.

188
00:11:47,394 --> 00:11:49,896
Why don't you give me something too?

189
00:11:51,148 --> 00:11:52,149
What?

190
00:11:53,025 --> 00:11:54,400
You want something of mine?

191
00:11:54,401 --> 00:11:58,321
Well, Mr. Jang is in my corner,
but the director is neutral.

192
00:11:58,322 --> 00:11:59,906
I don't feel safe.

193
00:12:00,157 --> 00:12:02,616
If Mr. Son gets something
from Mr. Jeong

194
00:12:02,617 --> 00:12:04,077
we'll all be in trouble.

195
00:12:05,078 --> 00:12:06,412
Let's plan long-term.

196
00:12:06,413 --> 00:12:09,374
Give me something good, okay?

197
00:12:09,958 --> 00:12:11,043
Thanks for the scarf.

198
00:12:13,587 --> 00:12:15,881
Everyone's dead anxious.

199
00:12:16,381 --> 00:12:19,259
Laknes is a done deal
because the director wants it

200
00:12:19,676 --> 00:12:21,511
but you're the only one
who'll do it without complaint.

201
00:12:22,012 --> 00:12:25,848
They want Kim as associate director,
but his sales aren't good enough

202
00:12:25,849 --> 00:12:28,518
so they're taking a few
of your brands to boost his numbers.

203
00:12:29,269 --> 00:12:33,190
And now Son is worried
he won't get promoted this time.

204
00:12:33,857 --> 00:12:39,029
And people think I don't care at all
who you give those brands to.

205
00:12:40,238 --> 00:12:42,115
Should I give you one too
if you're that upset?

206
00:12:43,325 --> 00:12:46,077
I'm just worried for the two of us.

207
00:12:46,078 --> 00:12:47,245
Don't give me anything.

208
00:12:48,205 --> 00:12:49,705
Here's how I feel.

209
00:12:49,706 --> 00:12:52,042
I want my brands to do better
at the new teams.

210
00:12:52,292 --> 00:12:55,002
It's like I want them to meet
a good adoptive family.

211
00:12:55,003 --> 00:12:58,047
Instead of letting them
take what's yours

212
00:12:58,048 --> 00:12:59,924
why don't you take a stand?

213
00:12:59,925 --> 00:13:02,844
"I can't take Laknes.
Let me secure my own sales."

214
00:13:04,221 --> 00:13:08,349
Even I think
only I can handle Laknes.

215
00:13:08,350 --> 00:13:09,725
You don't want it, either.

216
00:13:09,726 --> 00:13:12,354
Exactly, I don't even want to do it,
so why would you?

217
00:13:13,647 --> 00:13:16,107
Since we're on the topic,
think of your poor team.

218
00:13:16,108 --> 00:13:19,026
They take all the brands no one wants
and do all the hard work.

219
00:13:19,027 --> 00:13:21,737
Once the brands are on track,
they give them to someone else.

220
00:13:21,738 --> 00:13:22,864
What the heck is that?

221
00:13:24,032 --> 00:13:25,158
Are you consoling me or what?

222
00:13:25,951 --> 00:13:29,286
I feel sorry for you, that's all.
I really do.

223
00:13:29,287 --> 00:13:33,082
To be honest, no one cares about me

224
00:13:33,083 --> 00:13:35,252
but aren't you in Mr. Jang's camp?

225
00:13:36,086 --> 00:13:37,754
What's up with him?

226
00:13:38,130 --> 00:13:41,048
He should be responsible
for the employee he promoted.

227
00:13:41,049 --> 00:13:42,384
Why are you always suffering?

228
00:13:42,634 --> 00:13:44,219
Don't you think... What the heck?

229
00:13:45,262 --> 00:13:46,847
Gosh, that punk.

230
00:13:47,514 --> 00:13:48,598
Wait up.

231
00:13:52,144 --> 00:13:53,394
- You're leaving?
- Yes.

232
00:13:53,395 --> 00:13:54,396
Bye.

233
00:13:58,108 --> 00:13:59,860
- Take care, Gong.
- Bye.

234
00:14:10,412 --> 00:14:11,580
I'm heading out.

235
00:14:12,122 --> 00:14:13,290
Sure, bye.

236
00:14:15,542 --> 00:14:16,877
Wow, I'm starving.

237
00:14:17,335 --> 00:14:18,794
Let's eat. What do you want?

238
00:14:18,795 --> 00:14:22,673
How about the barbecue place
we went to last time?

239
00:14:22,674 --> 00:14:24,801
That place is too cheap,
and you're buying.

240
00:14:25,218 --> 00:14:26,470
Oh, am I buying?

241
00:14:27,095 --> 00:14:28,847
Will you join us, Mr. Gong?

242
00:14:30,557 --> 00:14:31,766
No, I'm fine.

243
00:14:32,058 --> 00:14:34,018
Okay, I'll head home, then.

244
00:14:34,019 --> 00:14:35,604
I'm leaving too, sir.

245
00:14:36,146 --> 00:14:39,148
- Let's have what Ji-hye wants.
- Ji-hye?

246
00:14:39,149 --> 00:14:40,649
What I want?

247
00:14:40,650 --> 00:14:41,860
She prefers pork.

248
00:14:42,611 --> 00:14:44,028
- She likes pork?
- Yes.

249
00:14:44,029 --> 00:14:45,864
Then we should go for somaek.

250
00:14:46,239 --> 00:14:48,991
- Somaek.
- Are we getting drunk again?

251
00:14:48,992 --> 00:14:50,660
Oh, sounds good.

252
00:14:57,751 --> 00:15:00,252
TRAIN IS APPROACHING

253
00:15:00,253 --> 00:15:01,880
STOP

254
00:15:08,470 --> 00:15:09,804
What did the doctor say?

255
00:15:10,472 --> 00:15:11,680
About your father.

256
00:15:11,681 --> 00:15:14,475
Oh, that? He got a few tests done.

257
00:15:14,476 --> 00:15:16,101
The results aren't out yet.

258
00:15:16,102 --> 00:15:17,978
But they said
it's nothing to worry about.

259
00:15:17,979 --> 00:15:19,396
Still, keep an eye on him.

260
00:15:19,397 --> 00:15:21,065
Older people aren't like
what you think.

261
00:15:21,066 --> 00:15:22,566
Okay, I'll do that.

262
00:15:22,567 --> 00:15:23,901
Tell me when you get the results.

263
00:15:23,902 --> 00:15:26,321
I can put you in touch
with a different hospital.

264
00:15:26,863 --> 00:15:27,948
You'd do that?

265
00:15:29,032 --> 00:15:30,033
Thank you.

266
00:15:31,618 --> 00:15:33,202
Are you busy, Ji-hye?

267
00:15:33,203 --> 00:15:34,328
No.

268
00:15:34,329 --> 00:15:35,830
Can you work the tongs, then?

269
00:15:36,331 --> 00:15:37,499
Oh, let me.

270
00:15:37,916 --> 00:15:40,042
I don't mind cooking the meat.

271
00:15:40,043 --> 00:15:42,629
Why? Is it because she's a woman?

272
00:15:43,296 --> 00:15:44,673
Or because she's a contract worker?

273
00:15:45,298 --> 00:15:47,592
No, it's not exactly that...

274
00:15:47,884 --> 00:15:51,763
Man or woman, contract or full-time,
Ji-hye is still family.

275
00:15:52,514 --> 00:15:53,515
Aren't you the youngest?

276
00:15:54,391 --> 00:15:57,644
Yes, I am. I should've
watched the grill. Sorry.

277
00:15:58,478 --> 00:16:00,397
I don't know what Gong's thinking

278
00:16:01,022 --> 00:16:04,359
but I don't plan to let her go
after her contract expires.

279
00:16:04,943 --> 00:16:06,860
- What?
- Just you wait.

280
00:16:06,861 --> 00:16:10,364
I brown-nose everyone
I see at work for a reason.

281
00:16:10,365 --> 00:16:12,074
I'm trying to secure an opening.

282
00:16:12,075 --> 00:16:14,619
I grovel and beg, just for you.

283
00:16:15,787 --> 00:16:18,664
I see. Thank you, Mr. Yang.

284
00:16:18,665 --> 00:16:20,833
If you're grateful,
flip the meat before it burns.

285
00:16:20,834 --> 00:16:21,918
Sorry.

286
00:16:22,210 --> 00:16:23,461
Let's drink.

287
00:17:14,971 --> 00:17:18,058
You have a great posture, Mr. Gong.

288
00:17:21,269 --> 00:17:22,811
Don't most office workers

289
00:17:22,812 --> 00:17:25,690
get tech-neck and crooked spines
after seven years?

290
00:17:26,441 --> 00:17:29,152
I have dry eyes and fatty liver,
and that's bad enough for me.

291
00:17:29,903 --> 00:17:30,904
You stayed late.

292
00:17:31,363 --> 00:17:33,406
This is early for me.

293
00:17:35,283 --> 00:17:36,368
You look good.

294
00:17:37,243 --> 00:17:38,912
I pretend to be good.

295
00:17:41,414 --> 00:17:42,415
Are you going home?

296
00:17:42,832 --> 00:17:44,124
I have plans.

297
00:17:44,125 --> 00:17:45,293
Let's get a drink.

298
00:17:45,835 --> 00:17:46,836
I have plans.

299
00:17:47,170 --> 00:17:48,963
Let's have pufferfish soup
and split the bill.

300
00:17:50,048 --> 00:17:51,591
I have plans, I said.

301
00:17:52,967 --> 00:17:54,761
You don't have plans.

302
00:17:57,430 --> 00:17:58,431
Hurry up.

303
00:18:00,767 --> 00:18:02,184
CHEONGJIN PUFFERFISH

304
00:18:02,185 --> 00:18:03,937
Ma'am, can we get another bottle?

305
00:18:04,479 --> 00:18:06,231
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

306
00:18:13,655 --> 00:18:16,908
Hey, why are you always alone?

307
00:18:17,450 --> 00:18:20,578
Other team leaders are
always with their minions.

308
00:18:22,038 --> 00:18:23,748
Your team leader
doesn't take you anywhere.

309
00:18:24,708 --> 00:18:26,626
I bet it's the same reason.

310
00:18:27,210 --> 00:18:28,586
Exactly.

311
00:18:28,878 --> 00:18:30,921
I'm asking
since I'm just a member of a team

312
00:18:30,922 --> 00:18:33,841
but you're a team leader.

313
00:18:33,842 --> 00:18:36,051
The head of Legal is equivalent
to a managing director

314
00:18:36,052 --> 00:18:37,553
so to be exact, you're above me.

315
00:18:37,554 --> 00:18:39,055
Can you just not?

316
00:18:39,806 --> 00:18:41,557
You treated
everyone from our year to beef

317
00:18:41,558 --> 00:18:43,767
because you made team leader.

318
00:18:43,768 --> 00:18:45,269
But you're an outcast
in your own team.

319
00:18:45,270 --> 00:18:47,187
You're always
out and about on your own.

320
00:18:47,188 --> 00:18:49,482
What was that brand called? Laknes?

321
00:18:50,150 --> 00:18:53,277
Why are you letting everyone
play you like a fiddle?

322
00:18:53,278 --> 00:18:55,155
What's the point
of being a team leader?

323
00:18:55,572 --> 00:18:59,700
The company has
a big picture for Laknes.

324
00:18:59,701 --> 00:19:03,163
I happen to be
in charge of the backdrop.

325
00:19:03,621 --> 00:19:06,582
Okay. Let's say that
about the company's big picture.

326
00:19:06,583 --> 00:19:09,335
Why is Mr. Yang drawing the picture
for your team?

327
00:19:10,211 --> 00:19:12,213
He's always out
with the two underlings.

328
00:19:12,922 --> 00:19:16,384
He's making you do all the work
while he plays team leader.

329
00:19:17,260 --> 00:19:19,262
I know he joined Hongsung before you

330
00:19:19,804 --> 00:19:21,264
but isn't that just wrong?

331
00:19:24,851 --> 00:19:25,977
Mr. Yang...

332
00:19:29,105 --> 00:19:31,191
- He gets on my nerves.
- Right?

333
00:19:32,150 --> 00:19:33,734
But part of me thinks

334
00:19:33,735 --> 00:19:36,988
even if he gets on my nerves
and plays team leader

335
00:19:37,947 --> 00:19:39,365
if he hits our goals

336
00:19:40,283 --> 00:19:43,495
and make things work,
isn't that good enough?

337
00:19:44,078 --> 00:19:45,914
We're all there to do a job.

338
00:19:46,623 --> 00:19:48,792
Is it all fine if things work out?

339
00:19:49,751 --> 00:19:51,211
You suffer.

340
00:19:51,544 --> 00:19:53,797
If my suffering means things work out

341
00:19:54,964 --> 00:19:55,965
it's all good.

342
00:19:56,800 --> 00:19:59,177
Is Hongsung a company or a temple?

343
00:19:59,803 --> 00:20:01,763
You might actually reach nirvana.

344
00:20:11,981 --> 00:20:14,275
See you. Take care at work.

345
00:20:14,526 --> 00:20:16,820
You're still talking about work?

346
00:20:17,111 --> 00:20:19,572
That's all you talk about.

347
00:20:21,032 --> 00:20:22,826
Is your workday not over yet?

348
00:20:23,701 --> 00:20:25,787
Jeez, Gong Eun-tae.

349
00:20:35,255 --> 00:20:36,297
Take care.

350
00:21:16,254 --> 00:21:18,423
What kind of life am I living?

351
00:21:36,024 --> 00:21:37,317
- Are you all right?
- Yes.

352
00:21:38,192 --> 00:21:40,445
- Let me help.
- No, leave it.

353
00:21:42,405 --> 00:21:43,823
I was born into a family

354
00:21:44,115 --> 00:21:46,117
that wasn't rich,
but wasn't poor, either.

355
00:21:48,036 --> 00:21:50,038
I could climb if I worked hard

356
00:21:50,747 --> 00:21:53,374
and I could fall
if I made one mistake.

357
00:21:54,208 --> 00:21:55,292
GONG EUN-TAE

358
00:21:55,293 --> 00:21:56,544
That's why I studied hard.

359
00:22:01,132 --> 00:22:03,509
I wanted to get
into a better college...

360
00:22:05,595 --> 00:22:07,889
and I wanted to get a better job.

361
00:22:15,438 --> 00:22:19,567
Regardless of the result,
working hard put me at ease.

362
00:22:20,818 --> 00:22:24,614
That's what made me think
I was living life well.

363
00:22:36,376 --> 00:22:39,379
That's how I got a job
at Hongsung International.

364
00:22:40,171 --> 00:22:42,757
They have the second-most turnover

365
00:22:43,174 --> 00:22:45,301
and the third most brands
in the industry.

366
00:22:45,843 --> 00:22:47,220
It's a large company

367
00:22:47,679 --> 00:22:50,181
with 900 employees
and annual sales of 800 billion won.

368
00:22:51,182 --> 00:22:53,434
My parents didn't know
the name of the company

369
00:22:53,810 --> 00:22:56,938
but they were proud
I worked at a large one.

370
00:22:57,605 --> 00:23:02,151
And I was grateful I could
support myself before I was too old.

371
00:23:03,778 --> 00:23:06,155
Nothing changed
after I started working.

372
00:23:07,281 --> 00:23:09,409
I remained in the same frame

373
00:23:10,535 --> 00:23:11,953
spending the same amount of time

374
00:23:13,204 --> 00:23:14,914
and did my best as always.

375
00:23:17,041 --> 00:23:18,501
For three whole years

376
00:23:19,877 --> 00:23:23,005
I was the first to come in
and the last to leave.

377
00:23:23,006 --> 00:23:24,298
So I got promoted
to assistant manager.

378
00:23:26,384 --> 00:23:28,970
Three more years of that,
and I made team leader.

379
00:23:56,998 --> 00:23:58,332
After all those years of work

380
00:23:58,833 --> 00:24:01,127
I can afford an efficiency apartment

381
00:24:02,837 --> 00:24:05,339
a slightly fatty liver, dry eyes

382
00:24:05,757 --> 00:24:07,633
and an almost slipped disk.

383
00:24:12,638 --> 00:24:14,098
Does everyone live like this?

384
00:24:17,018 --> 00:24:18,311
If I work a little harder

385
00:24:18,686 --> 00:24:20,438
will my life become a little better?

386
00:24:24,442 --> 00:24:27,111
For what did I live and work so hard?

387
00:24:34,702 --> 00:24:38,790
And when did I stop
living and working so hard?

388
00:24:46,756 --> 00:24:48,256
- Who is it?
- Hey.

389
00:24:48,257 --> 00:24:49,925
- Oh, hello.
- Hello.

390
00:24:49,926 --> 00:24:53,345
- I brought your dry-cleaning.
- Thank you.

391
00:24:53,346 --> 00:24:54,930
Oh, one more thing.

392
00:24:54,931 --> 00:24:58,225
I lost one of your dress shirts.

393
00:24:58,226 --> 00:24:59,310
- Did you?
- Yes.

394
00:25:01,395 --> 00:25:03,688
Which one did you lose?

395
00:25:03,689 --> 00:25:07,692
My wife only said it's in the ledger,
but she can't find it.

396
00:25:07,693 --> 00:25:09,487
I don't know which one it is.

397
00:25:09,862 --> 00:25:12,657
Then I guess...

398
00:25:13,282 --> 00:25:14,450
Have a good evening.

399
00:25:21,082 --> 00:25:24,877
And since when did I stop
getting angry?

400
00:25:30,299 --> 00:25:34,220
HANKYEONG BANK
EULJIRO 1-GA STATION

401
00:25:41,144 --> 00:25:42,311
Mr. Yang.

402
00:25:43,187 --> 00:25:44,688
Hi, Ju-hui.

403
00:25:44,689 --> 00:25:46,899
- Good morning.
- Morning.

404
00:25:48,151 --> 00:25:50,653
Why are you so down this morning?

405
00:25:51,154 --> 00:25:54,115
It's weird to be excited about work.
Beware of such people.

406
00:25:54,782 --> 00:25:58,077
Are you worried
about the brand shift?

407
00:25:59,829 --> 00:26:02,123
The brand shift? What do you mean?

408
00:26:02,832 --> 00:26:04,333
You haven't heard?

409
00:26:08,963 --> 00:26:10,715
- Morning.
- Hello.

410
00:26:13,009 --> 00:26:14,343
Good morning.

411
00:26:16,137 --> 00:26:17,972
- Mr. Yang.
- Hello.

412
00:26:18,556 --> 00:26:20,850
- Morning. Can you...
- Let's talk.

413
00:26:42,288 --> 00:26:44,832
What is this about?

414
00:26:45,291 --> 00:26:49,128
What's this about handing over
our brands to other teams?

415
00:26:53,132 --> 00:26:54,217
Stuff happened.

416
00:26:54,592 --> 00:26:55,676
Yes, but why?

417
00:26:58,137 --> 00:27:00,305
We have to launch Laknes.

418
00:27:00,306 --> 00:27:02,682
We have to start from scratch

419
00:27:02,683 --> 00:27:04,018
and it'll be a lot of work.

420
00:27:04,644 --> 00:27:09,315
So we have to pack up the brands
we were working on

421
00:27:10,691 --> 00:27:12,485
so other teams can take over.

422
00:27:14,528 --> 00:27:16,489
Don't you think that's too much?

423
00:27:18,241 --> 00:27:21,953
None of our previous brands
started off normal.

424
00:27:22,912 --> 00:27:23,955
Eynard?

425
00:27:25,498 --> 00:27:28,541
They made a decent amount,
and Team 3 couldn't handle it.

426
00:27:28,542 --> 00:27:30,753
So they were fine,
but what about the others?

427
00:27:31,837 --> 00:27:33,881
Weren't they all brands
that should've been dropped?

428
00:27:34,799 --> 00:27:37,467
We took them in and revived them

429
00:27:37,468 --> 00:27:38,718
only to lose them.

430
00:27:38,719 --> 00:27:41,430
Now we get Laknes
that flopped once already?

431
00:27:42,056 --> 00:27:44,475
Even if the team leader
doesn't have much clout

432
00:27:45,309 --> 00:27:47,478
that doesn't mean
they can walk all over the team.

433
00:27:50,773 --> 00:27:51,774
Mr. Yang.

434
00:27:53,567 --> 00:27:56,821
Do you think
I want to lose the brands

435
00:27:57,530 --> 00:27:59,532
I was working on?

436
00:28:00,658 --> 00:28:01,701
Mr. Gong.

437
00:28:02,868 --> 00:28:07,163
Can you please do
just one thing for me?

438
00:28:07,164 --> 00:28:09,375
Let us keep our projects.

439
00:28:09,667 --> 00:28:13,713
That's the least you can do
if you expect us to trust you.

440
00:28:14,505 --> 00:28:16,299
Is that so much to ask?

441
00:28:18,301 --> 00:28:21,178
Just let us do our job in peace.

442
00:28:22,096 --> 00:28:23,139
Please?

443
00:29:04,013 --> 00:29:05,348
Did Mr. Yang headbutt you?

444
00:29:07,433 --> 00:29:09,977
That stupid punk.

445
00:29:13,981 --> 00:29:15,316
He was right, though.

446
00:29:16,359 --> 00:29:18,903
A team leader is useless
if he loses his team's trust.

447
00:29:19,278 --> 00:29:21,989
So what? If Yang headbutted you

448
00:29:22,365 --> 00:29:23,407
what will you do?

449
00:29:24,033 --> 00:29:25,910
Shouldn't you headbutt someone too?

450
00:29:28,913 --> 00:29:31,165
Did you ever see me get angry?

451
00:29:32,249 --> 00:29:34,460
Have I seen you get angry?

452
00:29:35,294 --> 00:29:36,295
I haven't.

453
00:29:37,088 --> 00:29:38,756
I don't shout when I'm angry.

454
00:29:39,799 --> 00:29:42,843
If I do, I only have to sort out
that aftermath.

455
00:29:43,719 --> 00:29:47,180
No one cares about that
when they're angry.

456
00:29:47,181 --> 00:29:48,849
They just lash out.

457
00:29:52,686 --> 00:29:54,980
So what? What will you do now?

458
00:29:55,815 --> 00:29:57,191
I must do something.

459
00:29:58,067 --> 00:29:59,193
Like what?

460
00:29:59,652 --> 00:30:01,153
ASSOCIATE DIRECTOR'S OFFICE

461
00:30:09,453 --> 00:30:11,330
- Is he in?
- Yes.

462
00:30:23,843 --> 00:30:24,885
Come in.

463
00:30:33,269 --> 00:30:34,270
What is it?

464
00:30:34,854 --> 00:30:36,230
I have something to say.

465
00:30:36,522 --> 00:30:38,691
- Will it take a while?
- It might.

466
00:30:39,650 --> 00:30:40,651
Sit.

467
00:30:49,785 --> 00:30:50,786
What is it?

468
00:30:52,621 --> 00:30:53,998
It's about Laknes.

469
00:30:54,415 --> 00:30:56,208
Could you give it to another team?

470
00:31:00,254 --> 00:31:03,132
Is your team disheartened
about taking Laknes?

471
00:31:05,176 --> 00:31:06,469
Did Yang Jun-ho complain?

472
00:31:09,555 --> 00:31:11,097
Talk to me.

473
00:31:11,098 --> 00:31:14,351
He's the only subordinate
who would complain.

474
00:31:15,144 --> 00:31:18,147
Everyone agrees, though.

475
00:31:34,288 --> 00:31:35,289
Hey.

476
00:31:37,124 --> 00:31:39,001
Will you let them
control you forever?

477
00:31:40,669 --> 00:31:43,796
If you really can't do it,
then I'll accept that.

478
00:31:43,797 --> 00:31:45,299
I can give it to another team.

479
00:31:45,966 --> 00:31:47,134
But that's not the case.

480
00:31:47,843 --> 00:31:50,845
You can take it,
but one of your lackeys can't.

481
00:31:50,846 --> 00:31:53,724
Isn't that why you took a deep breath
before coming in to see me?

482
00:31:54,934 --> 00:31:57,478
Do you think I made you team leader
to take on easy jobs?

483
00:32:00,272 --> 00:32:02,525
No, I never thought so.

484
00:32:05,236 --> 00:32:07,446
Jeez, that's exactly what you think.

485
00:32:11,575 --> 00:32:14,036
It's easy to keep doing
what you're good at.

486
00:32:14,453 --> 00:32:16,621
As long as your brain works

487
00:32:16,622 --> 00:32:19,083
anyone can do that. However...

488
00:32:21,126 --> 00:32:23,170
It's hard to revive a dying brand.

489
00:32:24,338 --> 00:32:26,006
That's not for just anyone.

490
00:32:26,590 --> 00:32:29,468
I gave you the job
because I believe in you.

491
00:32:30,261 --> 00:32:31,887
Yes, it will be hard work.

492
00:32:32,388 --> 00:32:35,056
And your team will complain,
but what can I do?

493
00:32:35,057 --> 00:32:37,810
They pull off
what you tell them to do.

494
00:32:42,773 --> 00:32:43,774
Bear with it.

495
00:32:44,900 --> 00:32:47,528
And pull it off.

496
00:32:47,945 --> 00:32:49,196
It goes on your record.

497
00:32:54,493 --> 00:32:55,578
Get out of here.

498
00:33:22,354 --> 00:33:24,315
Darn it.

499
00:33:26,483 --> 00:33:27,942
- Gi-tae.
- Yes?

500
00:33:27,943 --> 00:33:30,529
- Let's go out for a smoke.
- Okay.

501
00:33:32,323 --> 00:33:33,782
Ji-hye, join us for some air.

502
00:33:34,533 --> 00:33:35,534
Okay.

503
00:33:36,201 --> 00:33:37,620
Jeez...

504
00:34:06,690 --> 00:34:09,734
PRESSED PORK HEAD MEAT

505
00:34:09,735 --> 00:34:11,862
KOREAN BEEF

506
00:34:16,325 --> 00:34:19,453
SEONGGYEONG BUTCHER

507
00:34:29,838 --> 00:34:30,964
SYSTEM IS DOWN

508
00:34:32,800 --> 00:34:33,801
SYSTEM IS DOWN

509
00:34:36,178 --> 00:34:38,180
Sorry, the checkout machine
isn't working.

510
00:34:39,056 --> 00:34:40,808
What should I do, then?

511
00:34:41,684 --> 00:34:42,810
Do you have cash?

512
00:34:43,644 --> 00:34:44,645
Yes.

513
00:34:48,607 --> 00:34:50,484
- Here.
- That's 10,000 won.

514
00:34:58,534 --> 00:34:59,868
We're out of change.

515
00:35:00,577 --> 00:35:01,829
I'll come by another time.

516
00:35:05,541 --> 00:35:06,959
Would you like to buy
a lottery ticket?

517
00:35:08,377 --> 00:35:09,378
Sorry?

518
00:35:09,670 --> 00:35:12,464
Two beers are 5,000 won,
and a ticket is 5,000 won.

519
00:35:15,801 --> 00:35:17,636
- Sure, give me one.
- Okay.

520
00:35:23,767 --> 00:35:24,852
Random numbers?

521
00:35:26,562 --> 00:35:27,563
Okay.

522
00:35:33,527 --> 00:35:34,945
Here you go.

523
00:35:42,786 --> 00:35:44,163
Do I get a plastic bag?

524
00:35:45,247 --> 00:35:47,040
You didn't pay 100 won for one.

525
00:36:26,538 --> 00:36:29,124
MOM

526
00:36:33,712 --> 00:36:34,838
Hello, Mom.

527
00:36:35,380 --> 00:36:36,590
Did you have dinner?

528
00:36:36,965 --> 00:36:38,800
I'm eating right now.

529
00:36:38,801 --> 00:36:40,344
Do you have any food at home?

530
00:36:40,719 --> 00:36:42,221
Should I send you some?

531
00:36:42,638 --> 00:36:45,389
I still have what you sent me
last time.

532
00:36:45,390 --> 00:36:47,433
I sent that a long time ago.

533
00:36:47,434 --> 00:36:48,560
You should eat it up quickly.

534
00:36:48,977 --> 00:36:52,397
Tell me if you ever need
any side dishes.

535
00:36:52,856 --> 00:36:54,649
I'll tell you if I do.

536
00:36:54,650 --> 00:36:57,027
Okay. Oh, there's one more thing.

537
00:36:57,277 --> 00:36:59,530
It's nothing serious.

538
00:37:00,155 --> 00:37:02,574
Can you give your brother
five million won?

539
00:37:04,493 --> 00:37:05,993
What is it this time?

540
00:37:05,994 --> 00:37:09,747
Your brother was on the night shift

541
00:37:09,748 --> 00:37:11,999
and some drunkards got into a fight.

542
00:37:12,000 --> 00:37:15,419
When Eun-seok tried to stop them,
one guy fell and hurt his back.

543
00:37:15,420 --> 00:37:18,464
He's demanding your brother
pay for the treatment

544
00:37:18,465 --> 00:37:19,799
but you know he's penniless.

545
00:37:19,800 --> 00:37:23,428
A security guard barely makes enough
after expenses and his kid's tuition.

546
00:37:23,929 --> 00:37:25,179
I'll give him a call.

547
00:37:25,180 --> 00:37:26,931
No, don't call him.

548
00:37:26,932 --> 00:37:29,351
He doesn't know I called you.

549
00:37:29,893 --> 00:37:31,270
He knows.

550
00:37:31,854 --> 00:37:33,230
I'll call him.

551
00:37:41,655 --> 00:37:43,407
GONG EUN-SEOK

552
00:37:44,408 --> 00:37:45,909
CALLING

553
00:37:46,535 --> 00:37:49,204
MY LITTLE BROTHER

554
00:37:58,797 --> 00:38:00,048
Hey, Eun-tae.

555
00:38:01,174 --> 00:38:02,175
You need money?

556
00:38:02,885 --> 00:38:04,970
Gosh, did Mom tell you?

557
00:38:05,846 --> 00:38:07,472
I told her not to tell you.

558
00:38:08,181 --> 00:38:09,724
Will five million won do?

559
00:38:09,725 --> 00:38:11,350
Yes, that'll be enough.

560
00:38:11,351 --> 00:38:13,728
I'll pay you back soon.

561
00:38:13,729 --> 00:38:14,855
When?

562
00:38:15,689 --> 00:38:17,190
What? When?

563
00:38:18,483 --> 00:38:20,192
When can I pay you back?

564
00:38:20,193 --> 00:38:21,444
Let me see...

565
00:38:21,445 --> 00:38:23,655
Do you know
how much I lent you so far?

566
00:38:25,407 --> 00:38:27,784
Just ask for it.
Why do you say you owe me?

567
00:38:28,535 --> 00:38:31,203
But I should pay you back.

568
00:38:31,204 --> 00:38:32,205
Eun-seok.

569
00:38:32,956 --> 00:38:36,418
Do you think everyone
with an office job can save up?

570
00:38:37,085 --> 00:38:38,462
I don't have much.

571
00:38:39,129 --> 00:38:42,174
Do you know how much it costs
to just live and breathe in Seoul?

572
00:38:44,468 --> 00:38:46,345
We're family, aren't we?

573
00:38:48,055 --> 00:38:49,222
If we can't help each other

574
00:38:50,474 --> 00:38:52,017
let's at least not burden each other.

575
00:38:54,186 --> 00:38:55,938
Okay. Sorry.

576
00:38:57,773 --> 00:39:00,525
- I'll wire it right now.
- Oh, thanks.

577
00:39:05,614 --> 00:39:06,697
TYPE YOUR PIN

578
00:39:06,698 --> 00:39:09,159
5,000,000 WON SENT TO GONG EUN-SEOK

579
00:39:51,243 --> 00:39:53,120
SUPPLEMENT FOR STOMACH LINING

580
00:40:57,726 --> 00:40:58,769
SWOOSH

581
00:41:21,166 --> 00:41:25,170
6 LOTTERY WINNERS THIS WEEK
EACH GETS 1.9 BILLION WON

582
00:41:42,687 --> 00:41:45,065
LOTTO
5609TH DRAWING

583
00:42:08,588 --> 00:42:12,342
CONGRATULATIONS
TOTAL WINNINGS: 1,977,507,240 WON

584
00:42:14,928 --> 00:42:19,850
THE ORDINARY JACKPOT

585
00:42:43,540 --> 00:42:45,834
I've had enough for the day.

586
00:42:46,334 --> 00:42:47,543
Are you going home?

587
00:42:47,544 --> 00:42:50,422
Yes, if I stay any longer,
I feel like I might die.

588
00:42:51,840 --> 00:42:52,924
I feel the same.

589
00:42:53,258 --> 00:42:54,633
Why are you still here?

590
00:42:54,634 --> 00:42:56,970
If I leave now, I'll die tomorrow.

591
00:42:57,888 --> 00:42:59,681
We all live one day at a time.

592
00:43:00,473 --> 00:43:02,225
Wrap it up quickly.

593
00:43:02,893 --> 00:43:03,894
Have a good night.

594
00:43:16,615 --> 00:43:20,076
THIS WEEK'S TASKS

595
00:44:31,398 --> 00:44:35,402
GOT OFF WORK YET?

596
00:44:40,615 --> 00:44:42,617
GONG EUN-TAE

597
